{#
    What an import did, as a partial.

        {{ include('@Dataflow/import/_report.html.twig', {report: report}) }}

    ⚠️ **Read `report.isDryRun` before wording the count.** After a dry run nothing was written, so
    a panel announcing "1 240 imported" is why someone runs the real import a second time.

    ⚠️ **`report.errorCount` is exact; `report.errors` is a sample of at most a hundred.** A file
    read with the wrong delimiter fails on every row, and keeping fifty thousand entries to render a
    page nobody reads is the defect the cap exists for — but a screen that shows only the sample
    implies the file had exactly a hundred problems, so the truncation is said out loud.

    ⚠️ **Every message goes through the translator.** A mapper's refusal is a translation KEY and a
    validator's is already-rendered text; `|trans` returns an unknown key unchanged, so the one call
    is right for both.
#}
{% if report.isDryRun %}
    <p class="text-sm text-sky-600 dark:text-sky-400 mb-4">
        <i class="fa-solid fa-circle-info"></i>
        {{ 'dataflow.import.result.dry_run'|trans({}, 'dataflow') }}
    </p>
{% endif %}

<div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-4 mb-6">
    <div class="panel p-4">
        <p class="text-xs uppercase text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400">{{ 'dataflow.import.result.imported'|trans({'%count%': report.imported}, 'dataflow') }}</p>
        <p class="text-2xl font-bold text-emerald-600">{{ report.imported }}</p>
    </div>
    <div class="panel p-4">
        <p class="text-xs uppercase text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400">{{ 'dataflow.import.result.skipped'|trans({'%count%': report.skipped}, 'dataflow') }}</p>
        <p class="text-2xl font-bold text-amber-600">{{ report.skipped }}</p>
    </div>
    <div class="panel p-4">
        <p class="text-xs uppercase text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400">{{ 'dataflow.import.result.errors'|trans({'%count%': report.errorCount}, 'dataflow') }}</p>
        <p class="text-2xl font-bold text-red-600">{{ report.errorCount }}</p>
    </div>
</div>

{% if report.errors is not empty %}
    <div class="panel p-4 mb-6">
        <ul class="space-y-1 text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">
            {% for error in report.errors %}
                <li>
                    <span class="text-xs text-slate-500 mr-2 font-mono">{{ error.record }}</span>
                    {{ error.message|trans({}, 'dataflow') }}
                </li>
            {% endfor %}
        </ul>
        {% if report.errorsWereTruncated %}
            <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 mt-3">
                {{ 'dataflow.import.result.truncated'|trans({'%count%': report.errors|length}, 'dataflow') }}
            </p>
        {% endif %}
    </div>
{% endif %}
